35mm, side-angle dolly, mid-shot of shoulders and torso.

Slow parallax move from front-left to front-right.

Action / Physics:

The turquoise backdrop ripples outward from the horse like a gentle wave through thick paint.

The horse’s body stays structurally rigid; only the surface paint subtly flexes.

FX:

Wavefronts in the paint, leaving faint trails of altered texture.

A few loose paint petals detach and spin slowly in the air.

Audio:

A deep, filtered “whomp” as each ripple passes.

Subtle stereo whoosh matching the camera glide.

S3 — EYE OF PIGMENT (2.5–3.7 s)

Camera / Lens:

100mm close-up on the eye, slight dolly-in.

Camera tilts subtly from below, heroic angle.

Action / Physics:

The eye remains perfectly shaped, no distortion.

Inside the iris, pigments swirl like slow galaxies of magenta, gold, and cyan.

A tiny highlight flares as if a spark ignites.

FX:

Micro-particles of paint drift out from the corner of the eye and vanish into the air.

Audio:

A crystal-like high chime glissando on the pigment swirl.

Low bass swell ramping up for the next scene.

S4 — MANE SURGE (3.7–5.0 s)

Camera / Lens:

24mm, rapid but smooth orbit around the head (¾ front view to ¾ rear).

Slight motion blur, cinematic.

Action / Physics:

The mane bursts outward in layered arcs of paint ribbons, like a slow-motion explosion.

Ribbons stretch but always snap back to their original thickness and curvature; no melting.

The head and neck remain anatomically tight and unchanged.

FX:

Paint trails in the air, thick enough to feel heavy.

A few big droplets break off and fall in slow arcs.

Audio:

Strong percussive hit when the mane surges.

Layered swooshes as ribbons whip through the air, panned with camera orbit.

S5 — WEIGHTED STEP (5.0–6.7 s)

Camera / Lens:

35mm, low side profile of the front legs and chest.

Dolly tracking the horse slightly as it takes a single powerful step forward.

Action / Physics:

The horse lifts one front leg in a controlled, realistic way.

Hoof descends and compresses the acrylic ground, creating a small crater then rebound.

A ring of paint ripples out from the impact in concentric waves.

FX:

Thick droplets shoot outward at ground level, then quickly settle.

Subtle splash reflections on the underside of the leg.

Audio:

Deep, punchy hoof impact with a low-end thump.

Gentle cracking/creaking of drying paint.

S6 — PAINT REALM REVEAL (6.7–8.7 s)

Camera / Lens:

18mm wide, slow crane up and back, revealing more of the scene.

Slight tilt down to keep the horse centered while revealing the environment.

Action / Physics:

We see a vast landscape of rolling acrylic dunes in turquoise and pastel tones.

The horse stands proud, mid-pose, stable and well-proportioned at the center.

Distant ripples move across the “sea of paint” as if echoing the earlier step.

FX:

Ambient floating flakes and petals of paint drifting in the air.

Soft glints of light on distant ridges.

Audio:

Music swells into a more heroic theme.

Wind-like whoosh, but with sticky, viscous undertones.

S7 — SHOCKWAVE KICK (8.7–11.5 s)

Camera / Lens:

28mm, dynamic ¾ front view, slightly low.

Camera pushes in as the horse rears slightly and delivers a strong forward kick with a front hoof.

Action / Physics:

The kick remains anatomically correct, no warped limbs.

When the hoof slams down, a massive circular shockwave of rainbow paint blasts out across the floor in slow motion.

The environment warps elastically around the shockwave, then relaxes.

FX:

Shockwave ring: raised ridge of paint racing outward, splashing droplets and flinging petals into the air.

Air itself seems to streak with pastel colors for a moment.

Audio:

Huge orchestral hit + sub-bass impact at the moment of contact.

Low-frequency rumble sustained as the shockwave spreads.

Short reverse cymbal swell leading into the impact.

S8 — ASCENT INTO COLOR (11.5–14.0 s)

Camera / Lens:

24mm, overhead crane pulling up into a semi-top-down view, then tilting up toward a bright, glowing sky of cyan.

Slight slow motion here.

Action / Physics:

The horse performs a single, graceful leap, but body proportions stay stable and realistic.

As it rises, small chunks of paint peel off into the air, becoming glowing flakes and ribbons.

By the top of the leap, the horse begins a controlled dissolve into pigment, but the silhouette remains readable until the last second.

FX:

Trails of pastel ribbons follow its motion, then fragment into thousands of particles.

Faint volumetric shafts of light through drifting pigment dust.

Audio:

Music reaches a soaring peak, with choir-like pads or long strings.

High chimes and gentle reverse reverb on the dissolve.

S9 — TITLE IN PIGMENT DUST (14.0–15.0 s)

Camera / Lens:

Static-but-drifting composition: virtual 50mm, locked on a soft, abstract cloud of pigment dust on a turquoise background.

Very gentle push-in.

Action / FX:

The dust swirls and assembles into faint letter-shapes.

Clean serif letters “PAINTBORN STALLION” appear, formed from paint particles, then glow slightly.

Audio:

Music resolves into a final sustained chord.

Very soft shimmer, then fade to silence at exactly 15.0s.